## Version 2.4.48 — 2026-10-01 — pietro gerletti

`distance.distributional` clamps at zero. One ulp of round-off was destroying
most of the distribution-consensus production run.

In unbound #1 the argmax pipeline produced 30/30 valid simulations in all five
scenarios while the distribution pipeline produced 4-9/30, and in four of five
not one survivor reached two thirds of the 1,095-day horizon. Both ran off the
same frozen table, same seeds, same resources, back to back in one invocation.

The failures were `ValueError: Probabilities are not non-negative` from
`population_model.py:176`, where `rng4.choice` is handed per-host
`fitness_score` as `p=`. The chain:

1. `d_P` is >= 0 by construction -- the consensus base is each column's argmax,
   so `P(ref) - P(l) >= P(ref) - P(chat)` at every position and the sum cannot
   fall below `-delta`. A lineage that IS the consensus reaches exactly 0 by
   near-total cancellation. In doubles that cancellation landed at
   -5.551115123125783e-17, one ulp near delta=1.701898852462236.
2. `F = phi*d + (1-phi)/n_act`. While phi < 1 the second term is ~1e-3 and
   swamps a 1e-17 negative. phi saturates at exactly 1 around day 200, the term
   becomes exactly 0, and F inherits the sign -- which is why the crashes come
   late and why four scenarios have no long runs at all.
3. The guard at `population_model.py:170` tests `fitness_sum > 0`. One host at
   -5.55e-17 among hundreds of positive scores passes it; numpy then validates
   each probability individually and raises.

`distributional` now returns `distance if distance > 0.0 else 0.0`, restoring
the invariant the maths already guarantees. Argmax is untouched: `hamming_iw`
returns a non-negative integer, `consensus_distance` dispatches to it whenever
`consensus_mode != 'distribution'`, and `update.py:26` is the only caller of
`distributional` in the codebase -- so every argmax result stays bit-identical.
The fitness floor at `update.py:44-45` and the per-weight clip at
`population_model.py:170` were considered and deliberately NOT applied: the
quantity is provably non-negative, so the source is the right place.

Effect on unbound #1: the argmax half stands, all 150 seeds. The distribution
half is void -- too few seeds, and those that survived are a biased sample of
short epidemics -- and must be rerun. The calibration stages run on argmax and
are unaffected, so NO recalibration: the frozen table is still good.

Verification in `tests/test_distributional_nonnegative.py`, replacing three
scratch diagnostics. Unit: the consensus scores exactly 0 rather than -1e-17; a
sweep over 7 weightings x 9 genomes finds no negative; an unmapped position
still costs exactly 1, so the clamp has not flattened real distances. Live, at
production parameters through the pipeline's own `build_exp_scenario_settings`:
6/6 seeds complete, against 1/6 before the clamp and 6/6 for argmax. The
pre-fix numbers were established by monkeypatching the clamp in, so the
diagnosis never depended on an unapproved edit. `test_consensus_distance.py`
(C8) still passes, including `d_P == d_H` on pure columns.

