## Version 2.4.47 — 2026-10-01 — pietro gerletti

The SLURM monitor reports on events instead of on a timer, and the
long-running report's threshold is low enough to fire again.

`run_seeded_simulations`' polling loop printed the `SimulationsStatus` line
whenever the status changed OR 17 seconds had passed, so an unchanged line was
reprinted every 17s for the whole run and buried the transitions that carry
information. The timer branch is gone: the line now prints only when a
simulation actually changes status, and carries a `[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS]`
stamp so the record says when each transition happened. The date is in the
stamp because calibration arrays run across midnight. New
`print_simulations_status(status)` holds the format, used by the loop and by
the final completion line; `last_printed` is gone with the timer.

`LONG_RUNNING_THRESHOLD_S` 3600 -> 300 and `LONG_RUNNING_REPORT_INTERVAL_S`
3600 -> 600. At an hour nothing had qualified for a long time: measured
`.started` -> `.completed` across unbound #1's 1,400 tasks, the slowest was
2,423 s (HIV_high; median 227 s, p95 1,217 s) and every other experiment's
maximum was under 900 s. The v2.4.41-43 speedups cut those a further ~6x. The
write path was never at fault -- 3,371 `.progress` files on disk, one per
`.started` in every experiment, contents current (`{"time": 1062.5,
"final_time": 1095, "infected": 70}`) -- and `report_long_running_simulations`
prints nothing at all when nothing qualifies, so a correct silent report was
indistinguishable from a broken one.

Verification in `tests/test_status_reporting.py`, driving the real
`run_seeded_simulations` over a scripted status sequence with the Slurm-facing
calls stubbed: 40 unchanged polls produce one line rather than 40, a sequence
with two transitions produces exactly three lines (including the completion
one), every line is timestamped within 5 s of now, the payload is unchanged,
and the thresholds are asserted against the measured task runtimes rather than
against themselves.

Both pipeline runners dropped status lines from the saved log via
`re.compile(r'^SimulationsStatus\(')`; that pattern is removed from
`run_impact_long_shedders_pipeline.py` and
`run_impact_long_shedders_unbound_pipeline.py`. It existed because the 17s
reprint spammed the log; now that the line prints once per transition and
carries a timestamp, it IS the log's record of when each simulation moved, so
the archived log gains that record. `submitted N seeded simulations` is still
dropped. The test asserts both the kept and the dropped case against the real
`_is_slurm_monitor_noise` in both runners.

