## Version 2.4.37 — 2026-09-23 — pietro gerletti

Figure shape-and-storytelling pass, plus a third instance of the
wrong-data-source bug. These figures are for developing the argument, NOT
final -- both pipelines get rerun with final numbers afterwards.

**Figure 3 C/D read 6 standard genomes against 1,494 long-shedder ones.**
`_long_shedder_sequenced_genomes` took every intra-host lineage of every long
shedder, while `_standard_sequenced_genomes` took only the DIAGNOSIS-sequenced
standards. At the production `sequencing_rate = 0.05`, one unbound HIV_high
seed yields 7 sequences in total out of 1,521 infected individuals -- so the
sequence-space PCA showed a single colour, and the "excess divergence" panel
was comparing a within-host diversity cloud against a handful of surveillance
samples. Both types now read the COMPLETE intra-host record via one
`_ih_lineage_genomes()`: 2,692 standard and 1,494 long-shedder genomes per
seed. Subsampling caps apply to both sides instead of one.
**This is a data-source decision, not just a fix** -- the panels now describe
the diversity each host type CARRIES rather than what surveillance DETECTS.
Flagged in BACKLOG for re-checking before the final figures.

* **Pair sampling no longer materialises the product.** With the full pools a
  seed holds ~2.7k x 1.5k possible cross pairs, and the old code built all ~4M
  tuples (and ~3.6M within-pairs) before discarding all but 200. Indices are
  sampled directly now.
* **Figure 3 panel B: PCA replaced by the four raw metrics.** PC1/PC2 had no
  units and no stated loadings, so the only readable statement was "control
  clusters, the rest spread" -- it could not say which metric separated them.
  Now one small panel per metric, scenario on the x-axis, median bar per group.
* **New Figure 3S** (`fig3S_save.py`): clade-origin pies for every scenario
  side by side, so the trend across long-shedder burden is visible rather than
  asserted. Built on `plot_figures.py::build_figure_4`, reusing
