  data access changed, from the old (M, ratio, tau, R) master-log sweep to the
  current named scenarios.

**Figure 1:**

* One figure-level legend below the panels, replacing the per-axes ones.
  Entries name the modelled scenario with its clinical category in brackets --
  "SOT (solid organ transplant)", "Edge case (>300 d shedding)" -- because
  panel C's categories stand in for the modelled scenarios and now share their
  colours. The edge-case entry appears whenever EITHER the scenario exists or
  panel C holds >300 d patients, so the bound arm still explains its pink.
* Palette unified on Okabe-Ito. Patient data moved to bluish green `#009E73`,
  a hue no scenario uses, plus a dashed line -- previously it was dark blue
  against Control's near-black, effectively indistinguishable, and identical
  in greyscale.
* Panels B and C y-limit 800 -> 600. Regression lines extend to the panel edge
  rather than stopping at each series' own data maximum.
* Fit annotations gated behind `fig1_plots.SHOW_FIT_STATS` / `--no-fit-stats`,
  since the submission version will not show them.

**Figures 2-4:**

* **Seed is now in the output filename.** Rendering a second seed silently
  overwrote the first, which made comparing seeds impossible. Figure 1 is
  unaffected -- it aggregates over all seeds.
* **Figure 4 node markers 20 -> 4.** Size 20 was set for a four-tree layout;
