  30** (bound SOT). The panel reported SOT at **0.00022 s/s/y** against a
  0.00205 target -- the model missing by 9x -- with R2=0.11. It is not:
  `extract_ih_regression_data` over the same output gives **0.00202**.
  Replaced with that function, the one `cal_1` and the sanity plots already
  use, deleting ~50 lines of bespoke extraction rather than adding any. Point
  counts went from 19 to 6,925 (SOT), 22,598 (HIV) and 14,788 (edge_case).
  Textbook instance of the trap in CLAUDE.md: a healthy-looking panel
  measuring a different quantity from the one its title claims.
* **Seven panels became five.** The old layout split each clock across a data
  panel and a model panel (D/F for the global clock, E/G for the intra-host
