## Version 2.4.35 — 2026-09-18 — pietro gerletti

(2.4.34 landed only `Data/RealWorldData/` and the `.gitignore` rule -- a
`git add` with a stale pathspec failed silently and staged nothing else.
This entry covers the whole change; 2.4.35 carries the code.)

Figure 1's real-world inputs are now in the repo, the plotting job runs
against a chosen pipeline arm, and there is one command to bundle both paper
runs for download. Plus a packaging bug that has been corrupting every
archive this repo has ever produced.

* **`pixz -t` is not a test flag, and "integrity verification" was destroying
  the archives.** `package_simplicity_data.sh` ran `pixz -t "$archive"` to
  verify each archive; in pixz, `-t` means *"don't assume input is in tar
  format"* -- a compression flag. Every archive was therefore silently
  re-compressed to `<name>.tar.xz.xz` and the original deleted, while the
  script printed `SUCCESS: Packaging and verification complete.` The result
  needed `pixz -d` run twice to open and could not be read by plain
  `tar -xf` or `xz -d` at all. Confirmed in isolation: `pixz -t v.tar.xz`
  turns it into `v.tar.xz.xz`. Now `pixz -l`, which lists the tarball index
  -- a genuine read-only check that the file is valid xz *and* a readable
  tar. The verification glob also no longer silently passes when it matches
  nothing, and the success message prints the extract command. Verified end
  to end: a single `tar -I pixz -xf` now restores everything.
* **`Data/RealWorldData/`** holds Figure 1's three curated inputs --
  `data_fig1_D.csv` and `data_fig1_E.csv` (moved from the repo root) and
  `literature_long_shedders_data.csv`, the literature extraction panel C
  needs and which had never been in the repo at all. `.gitignore` gains
  `!Data/RealWorldData/` to escape the blanket `Data/*`. Figure 1 is now
  reproducible from a clean checkout.
* **Figure 1's inputs are resolved from the script's location, not the
  working directory.** All three were bare relative paths, so every one
  vanished if a figure ran from anywhere but the repo root -- and only panel
  C said so on the plot; D and E just went blank. Each now warns by full path
  when missing, and panel C reports how many patients and categories it
  loaded. Verified by running from `/tmp`: 123 patients / 9 categories, 1638
  and 259 rows.
* **`submit_plots.sh` would have failed on every figure.** It passed no
  `--exp-num`, which v2.4.33 made required, and it hardcoded
  `/home/gerlep93/miniconda3` for conda activation while recent pipeline logs
  run under a different HPC account. Now takes
  `<exp_num> [exp_name] [figure] [seed] [format]`, activates conda the
  portable way every other submit script in this repo already used, and
  creates all four log directories rather than only the one selected.
* **New `scripts/archive_paper_runs.sh`**: one command to bundle both paper
  runs -- bound `#7` and unbound `#1` by default -- with their pipeline logs,
  artifact zips, figures and the real-world inputs, plus a manifest recording
  commit, branch, host and date. Prints the archive path, its size and an
  `scp` line. Staging uses **hard links, not symlinks**: the packager's
  `tar -I pixz -cf` has no `--dereference`, so a symlinked staging tree would
  have archived the links and none of the data.

