## Version 2.4.24 — 2026-08-26 — pietro gerletti

The k_v A/B test (2.4.22) didn't confirm the k_v hypothesis: control/SOT
calibrated near-identically under k_v=0 vs 0.1, and HIV_low actually fit
*worse* at k_v=0. What tracked the failure cleanly in both arms was
`tau_3_long`, independent of k_v -- pointed at the measurement, not the
mechanism. Traced Stage 1's calibration fit
(`long_nsr_calibration_plot.py`) to using the same population-pooled,
global-reference, absolute-time regression as the "global clock" (just
filtered to long-shedder rows) -- not a genuine intra-host measurement,
unlike `plot_sot_sanity_regressions.py`'s `load_intrahost_long_data`,
which already resolved each host's own founder genome and own-infection-
relative time correctly.

* New `simplicity.tuning.evolutionary_rate.extract_ih_regression_data`:
  the shared, correct intra-host point extraction (own founder genome via
  `inherited_lineage`, time since own infection via `ih_birth -
  t_infection`, full `IH_lineages_trajectory`) -- consolidates what used
  to be two implementations (`plot_sot_sanity_regressions.py`'s own copy,
  now deleted, ~90 lines) into one.
* `long_nsr_calibration_plot.py`'s Stage 1 fit now fits each seed's
  genuine intra-host clock via this function, instead of the population-
  pooled regression. **This alone wasn't enough**: `impact_long_shedders_
  cal_2.py` had its own *separate* re-derivation of the same Stage 1
  value (`compute_long_nsr_per_tau`, reading the same raw simulation
  output independently) -- the one that actually reached
  `nsr_calibration_table.csv` -- still on the old method. Fixed there too,
  then eliminated the duplication at the root: `plot_and_fit_long_nsr_
  calibration` now persists its result (`write_calibrated_long_nsr`, in
  the experiment's `Fit_results/`), and cal_2.py reads it back
  (`read_calibrated_long_nsr`) instead of recomputing -- one
  implementation, one computation, and cal_2 now raises loudly if its own
  `--target-osr-long` doesn't match what the file was actually calibrated
  against.
* `edge_case` scenario removed from `SCENARIOS` (commented out, not
  deleted): at `tau_3_long=350.23`, raw-Hamming-distance saturation
  (~0.34 expected substitutions/site by end of window) and more
  transmission generations elapsing within cal_1's own isolated
  population both made its long-NSR calibration unreliable relative to
  SOT/HIV_low/HIV_high. `NSR_RANGES['cal1_long_nsr']['max']`: 0.5 -> 0.1.
* `Population.detect_sod_outliers`: IQR statistical-outlier pass now
  gated behind `use_iqr=False` (off by default; hard floor unchanged) --
  at the seed counts calibration sweeps actually run with (5-20), a
  Tukey fence over 3-5 points was too easily thrown off by the same
  single bad seed it was meant to catch.
* Minor: fixed a stale SLURM-mem comment (said 2G, actual default is 4G
  since 2.4.23's OOM fix), three stale "4x2 sanity grid" references (now
  3x2 after the edge_case removal), and a plot-legend label that silently
  collapsed the shared HIV_low/HIV_high tau=94.23 group to just
  "HIV_low" -- now "HIV_low+HIV_high".

